 <p>Consonant sounds occur in languages as single consonants, or as doubled=
, or as clustered combinations. Single consonant sounds are isolated by wor=
d boundaries or by intervening vowel sounds from other consonant sounds. Do=
ubled consonant sounds are either lengthened like <span class=3D"c3">[s]</s=
pan> in English =E2=80=9Chiss=E2=80=9D, or repeated like <span class=3D"c3"=
>[k]</span> in English =E2=80=9Cbackcourt=E2=80=9D. Consonant clusters cons=
ist of two or more single or doubled consonant sounds in a group, each of w=
hich is different from its immediate neighbor. In Lojban, doubled consonant=
s are excluded altogether, and clusters are limited to two or three members=
, except in Lojbanized names.</p>
